  "caveats": [
    "Feature-space attack: it edits the 54 numbers, not a real binary. Header edits are shown to be expressible on a real benign file, but not every tier's edit combination was built into a working malware executable.",
    "ImageBase changes need a relinked binary, base relocations, or a wrapper; a pre-built no-relocation executable cannot simply be rebased.",
    "Donor values come from the same distribution the model was recently fixed on; a model retrained on these donors would see them as benign, which is the point of an attacker copying them."
  ]
